From 10587b8b8f97c0a36f6e1c7c44b5d2634a98865c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:45:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hub): fix card overflow bug and remove stray committed
 patch files

The Fun Fact card (and any card with a long subtitle sentence, unlike
the short word/phrase subtitles on the other 5 cards) was overflowing
past the right edge of the screen instead of wrapping within its grid
column - visible as the card's border and text extending off-screen in
the reported screenshot.

HubCard's title/subtitle container had no min-w-0, and the subtitle
text itself had no wrapping constraint, so a long sentence could force
the card wider than its 2-column grid cell. Added min-w-0 to both the
grid cell wrapper and the title/subtitle container, truncate on the
title, and break-words + line-clamp-2 on the subtitle, so long content
always wraps and clips within the card instead of pushing it wider.

Also removes three .patch files that got committed into the repo root
as tracked files by a previous commit (should never have been checked
in - they're generated patches, not source), and adds *.patch to
.gitignore to stop it happening again.
