-Subject: [PATCH] fix(hub): fix quiz-unlock bypass, layout clipping, and card
- collision
-
-Six issues on the Learn Hub screen:
-
-1. Quiz unlocking prematurely ('directly doing 6th card' opened the
-   quiz): three separate bypasses of the 'all 6 categories complete'
-   requirement, all fixed to use the same strict, per-sub-card signal
-   (completedCategoriesCount / cardVisits) that the UI already displays:
-   - handleMainCardDone() only checked currentMainCardIndex === 5 before
-     routing straight to the quiz, regardless of whether categories 1-5
-     were actually done. The 'Take the Quiz!' button label had the same
-     bug. Both now check completedCategoriesCount(...) === 6.
-   - The /state/$slug/quiz route's loader guard used the older
-     cardsDone()/p.cards signal, which only required each category's
-     *main* card to have been opened once (not every sub-card in it) -
-     a weaker bar than what the hub UI enforces. Switched to
-     completedCategoriesCount for consistency.
-   - The Journey Map's internal 'quiz' view (view-state based, not a
-     real route) had no guard at all. Added an effect that bounces back
-     to the hub if reached before all 6 categories are complete.
-
-2. 'Your state adventure' progress card getting cropped: it lived
-   inside an overflow-y-auto scroll container with a negative top
-   margin pulling it up to overlap the header. The scroll container
-   clipped that overlap at its own top edge. Moved it to be a
-   non-scrolling sibling of the header instead.
-
-3. Completion checkmark overlapping the category icon: both were
-   fighting for the same top-right corner of each HubCard (checkmark
-   absolutely positioned there, icon pushed there via ml-auto in the
-   same row). Checkmark now renders on its own layer at the card level;
-   icon moved into the top row next to the numbered badge.
-
-4. All 6 cards + quiz card now fit on one screen without scrolling:
-   removed the scroll container, shrank the header, and compacted the
-   progress strip, card grid (now a fixed grid-rows-3 filling a flex-1
-   area), and quiz panel.
-
-Toast alignment (reported as left-aligned) was investigated but not
-changed - the current code already centers it explicitly
-(BottomToast.tsx), so a screenshot is needed to find whatever this
-actually is before changing anything.
