-Subject: [PATCH] fix(quiz): fix Rules-of-Hooks violation in QuizScreenContent
- (React #300/#310)
-
-commit b067e44 moved the 'states not loaded yet' early return from the
-QuizScreen wrapper into QuizScreenContent itself, placing it before 9
-more hook calls (useMemo, useEffect, and 7x useState). Whenever states
-was empty on a render, the component returned after only 3 hooks; once
-states populated on a later render, it called 12 total hooks. That
-mismatched hook count between renders is exactly what triggers minified
-React error #300/#310 ('Rendered fewer hooks than expected').
-
-Moves the loading check back to QuizScreen (the wrapper), which decides
-whether to mount QuizScreenContent at all - conditionally mounting a
-different component is safe, an early return partway through one
-component's hooks is not.
-
-Also fixes a divergence this introduced: the learn-hub quiz entry point
-(state.$slug.quiz.tsx) already navigates straight to /state/$slug/learn
-on completion, but the journey-map's embedded quiz entry point
-(JourneyMapScreen in screens.tsx) still routed to the now-unused
-quiz-done screen. Both entry points now behave the same way.
